 “slot-based” concurrency system:

At any time, there are at most MAX_CONCURRENCY jobs being processed.

Each job is copied from MinIO into input_files/.

A separate monitoring thread watches output_files/ for completed videos.

When a job completes, the monitor signals the main thread to fetch the next job from the queue — but total running jobs never exceed MAX_CONCURRENCY.

Jobs are allocated only as needed, not all at once.

